  "content": {
    "title": "How and where to watch 2026 NBA play-in tournament games on streaming",
    "text": "April 14, 2026, 6:21 a.m. ETAs the 82-game regular season grind comes to a close, the 2026 NBA postseason kicks off with play-in tournament games starting Tuesday, April 14.The Nos. 7-10 seeds in both the Western and Eastern Conference are set to compete in the play-in tourney, which will ultimately decide which teams move into the playoff bracket proper as the No. 7 and No. 8 seeds to face the top two seeds in each conference.The Oklahoma City Thunder and San Antonio Spurs await the outcomes of the play-in games in the West, while the Detroit Pistons and Boston Celtics wait for their matchups in the East.Here's a look at how to watch this year's play-in games, including how the play-in tournament works in practice.What is the NBA play-in tournament format?In each conference, the No. 7 and No. 8 seeds play against each other. The winner of that game moves on and becomes the No. 7 seed in the full playoff bracket to face the No. 2 seed in each conference.The No. 9 and No. 10 seeds also play against each other, with the winner moving on to face the loser of the 7-8 matchup. The loser of the No. 9 vs. No. 10 seed game is eliminated.Whoever wins the following game moves on as the No. 8 seed in the full playoff bracket to face the No. 1 overall seed in each conference.How and when to watch NBA play-in tournament gamesNBA play-in tournament games begin on Tuesday, April 14. All play-in tournament games will be streaming exclusively on Amazon Prime Video.Watch NBA play-in tournament games on PrimeNBA play-in tournament schedule 2026Tuesday, April 14:Miami Heat vs. Charlotte Hornets, 7:30 p.m. ET, loser eliminated from playoff contentionPhoenix Suns vs. Portland Trail Blazers, 10 p.m. ET, winner becomes No. 7 seed in Western Conference to face San Antonio SpursWednesday, April 15:Philadelphia 76ers vs. Orlando Magic, 7:30 p.m. ET, winner becomes No. 7 seed to face the Boston CelticsGolden State Warriors vs. Los Angeles Clippers, 10 p.m. ET, loser eliminated from playoff contentionThursday, April 16:TBD vs. TBD (Eastern Conference play-in for No. 8 seed), 7:30 p.m. ETTBD vs. TBD (Western Conference play-in for No. 8 seed), 10 p.m. ET",
